# Intent: the device side of the unit's own sounds (owner approved 2026-11-13). (1) The seven new earcons (Ogg Opus mono 16 kHz 24 kbps, 0.4 to 1.0 s, 0.5 to 3 KB each, rendered by body/scripts/render_unit_sounds.py as one soft-bell family: rising for good news, falling for bad) are embedded in the app image through main/CMakeLists.txt (recipe.sh copies them into assets/sfx); not in the assets partition, because the first-setup cue plays before the assets are applied and a file in the image cannot be missing at run time. (2) New MCP tools: self.audio.play_sound {name, urgent, test} plays one of the twelve fixed names through the gate (refused when muted, switched off or at night, with the safety cues exempt; test skips the off switch and the night rule but never the mute) and answers {ok} or {ok:false,error}; self.audio.set_sound_policy {enabled, night_ok, muted, dark, quiet_from, quiet_to} stores the policy in the unit's own NVS namespace mp_sounds (written only on a real change; dark is never saved), so quiet hours still work with the host down because the unit judges them on its own clock; self.audio.sound_info reports the policy, whether it is night, the link state, how many of the sixteen offline clips are in the assets and the play counts. (3) A weak maipai_mute_active() hook, false here, that the hard mute work overrides. Volume is the speaker volume already set by the host (bodies/stackchan/volume.py); nothing here changes it.
# Upstream: new files hal/maipai_sounds.h and hal/maipai_sounds.cc (MIT); m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/CMakeLists.txt, hal/hal.cpp, hal/hal_mcp.cpp (MIT). Applies after 115.
# Check after a flash: host log shows no "add" error; self.audio.play_sound {"name":"plug_in","test":true} plays two rising notes and answers {"ok":true}; {"name":"nope"} answers unknown_sound; set_sound_policy with muted=true then play_sound answers muted; sound_info shows clips_present 16 once the assets image is flashed with it.
